<% content_for :full_bleed, "1" %>
<% content_for :title, "About — Pharma Transport" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "Pharma Transport is built by Thomas Information Technology in Phoenix, Arizona, to give pharmaceutical transport a real chain-of-custody record instead of reconstructed paperwork." %>

<section class="border-b border-line bg-gradient-to-b from-[#fbfcfd] to-[#f3f6f8]">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-[76px] flex flex-col gap-4">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1 class="text-[38px]">A real chain-of-custody record, instead of paperwork rebuilt after the fact.</h1>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-ink-soft">
      Pharmaceutical transport generates a lot of documentation that only gets looked at when
      something goes wrong. Pharma Transport exists to make that record real from the start.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 flex flex-col gap-11">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    <h2 class="text-[22px]">What we do</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft text-[15.5px]">
      GPS tracking, custody handoffs, and delivery signatures are logged as they happen and
      turned into FDA-ready documentation automatically &mdash; not reconstructed from memory
      when a regulator, a client, or an auditor asks for a record that is supposed to exist.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    <h2 class="text-[22px]">Who&rsquo;s behind this</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft text-[15.5px]">
      Pharma Transport is built by <strong>Brett Thomas</strong> through Thomas Information
      Technology, based in Phoenix, Arizona. Brett was born and raised in Arizona, with an IT
      background and an education in Maricopa County. This is a solo-founder, hands-on build:
      the product, the compliance documentation, and the infrastructure it runs on are all
      built and maintained directly, not outsourced.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    <h2 class="text-[22px]">Where things stand</h2>
    <p class="text-ink-soft text-[15.5px]">
      This is an early-stage product: live in production, with real signup, real billing, and a
      real security posture &mdash; built to be trusted with the kind of documentation
      pharmaceutical transport actually needs, not a demo. If you want more detail on where
      things stand or how it works,
      <%= link_to "get in touch", new_user_registration_path %>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 border-t border-line pt-8">
    <% [
      ["Phoenix, AZ", "Where it’s built and run"],
      ["Solo founder", "Product, compliance, infrastructure"],
      ["In production", "Real signup, billing, and 2FA today"],
    ].each do |stat, label| %>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
        <span class="font-serif text-[22px]"><%= stat %></span>
        <span class="text-[13px] text-ink-faint"><%= label %></span>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-brand-700 text-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-15 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-6" style="padding-top:3.75rem;padding-bottom:3.75rem;">
    <h2 class="text-[24px] text-white">Want to see how it works?</h2>
    <div class="flex gap-3">
      <%= link_to "Sign up", new_user_registration_path, class: "btn", style: "background:#fff;color:#1f3a53;" %>
      <%= link_to "See pricing", pricing_path, class: "btn btn-secondary", style: "border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.3);color:#fff;background:transparent;" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
